{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Follow-up experiments complete (total Bedrock spend $91.15/$100). Exp A — Nova Pro as frontier slot, end-to-end review-plan replays in an isolated copy: 5/5 comparable tickets matched recorded verdicts (4 PASS, 1 BLOCK incl. same blocking finding), finder-slot cost $0.07-0.09 vs $2.31-3.00 recorded (~30-40x); agentic tool-looping works with a MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS entry (10k) and ~7% retryable tool_call flake; the agentic Pass-2 verifier runs on the STANDARD slot so a frontier swap does not touch it; overlap-judge 48k bug reproduced again (live). Exp B — completion-verifier gold set (differential vs Sonnet baseline 16/22 incl. 3-case fixture artifact): Haiku 16/22 zero false-accepts; Nova 2 Lite 14/22 zero false-accepts (over-strict on injection case); Nova Pro DISQUALIFIED (3 false-accept epochs on operator-attestation cases). Banked-run median cost: sonnet $1.20 → haiku $0.40 → nova-2-lite $0.027. Per-AC splitting is strictly dominated (~4.5x at any tier; already built+measured+deleted per 2948) — swap the model inside the banked design instead. Full data: reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786461567404530001,"uuid":"bc6e592d-1bf2-4f97-91df-ba7e4db7ef11"}